#!/usr/bin/env sh

# Reason: the two apps keep separate copies of every Mongoose model. When they drift,
# the app with the narrower copy cannot WRITE the fields it does not declare, and a
# missing enum value rejects the write outright. Both failures are silent, so they are
# caught here rather than in production.
#
# If this blocks you: run `npm run check:mirrors:list` to see the detail. Add the
# missing field or enum value to the copy that lacks it - only ever add. If the
# difference is deliberate, record it in tools/model-mirror/allowlist.ts with a reason.
npm run check:mirrors

# Reason: admin routes import main-app files directly, and inside the admin build
# "@/" resolves to apps/admin. A main-app module that reaches a "@/" path the admin
# app does not own compiles fine here and fails `next build` over there, which
# surfaces as a server that will not start rather than as a code error.
#
# If this blocks you: change the offending import to a relative path so it always
# finds the main app's own module, or mirror the module into apps/admin.
npm run check:cross-app
